Yes — this is what Prisma calls a **composite type**, but it's **MongoDB-only**.

You'd define it like:
```prisma
model User {
  id      String  @id @default(auto()) @map("_id") @db.ObjectId
  name    String
  address Address
}

type Address {
  country String
}
```

Source: `apps/docs/content/docs/orm/v7/prisma-schema/data-model/models.mdx` § "Defining composite types (MongoDB)" — note `@id`, `@unique`, `@relation` aren't supported inside `type` blocks. If you're on PostgreSQL/MySQL/etc., there's no equivalent — you'd need `Json` field or a real relation.

